nsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\n| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\n\n## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\n| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\n| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\n| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n\n## M4 — Standards, sectors and company variation\n\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\n| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\n| MC21 | Represent banks' liabilities, assets, deposits, capital and regulatory/economic constraints. U1, U2. | Define core bank structural records now and operation-level later methods for funding, credit, liquidity and capital, including accounting/prudential reconciliation and an appropriate worked case. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 specifies bank origination, transfer, interest, allowance, cash funding and default; exact fixture balances and capital reconciliation pass. Prudential weights are illustrative; full allowance lifecycle, IFRS 9/CECL and jurisdictional capital rules remain open. G7, G8. |\n| MC22 | Represent insurers' contract groups, claims, service/finance components, assets and reinsurance. U1, U2. | Define cohort/group state and movements, declared measurement approaches and interfaces, reinsurance links and a complete structural/roll-forward example; expand actuarial/accounting support. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` give a complete short-duration PAA gross/reinsurance roll-forward and chain-ladder point calculation. Selected AASB 17 paragraphs and Mack technical sections inspected. Separate treaty PAA eligibility and recognition timing are explicit in Version 1.2; journal counterexamples vary transferred risk and non-performance independently. General measurement, transition, variable fees and uncertainty/RA estimation remain open. G7, G8, G16. |\n\ndocs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md:28:DemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\ndocs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md:29:The single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\ndocs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md:45:accelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\ndocs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md:64:say Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\ndocs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md:114:report mappings, records/arrays/field access, finite choices, nonlinear bound\ndocs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md:116:currency/calendar variants, rounded or period observations, source conflicts and\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:9:restricted posting effect. Economic forecasting algorithms can live in typed\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:10:plugins; unrestricted numerical code does not need to be reimplemented in\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:55:\\code{Choice<E>} & A finite structural choice over enumeration E. No probability\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:70:error or numerical status and the rounding used when posting money.\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:134:alternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:135:alternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:143:endpoints exhaust it. Requesting the parent family's exact bounds produces\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:145:conditional run of \\code{allFixed} supplies $\\alpha=1$. Requesting a weighted\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:151:period and type. If the evidence is rounded, \\code{value(debt)} denotes a\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:170:  let charge = roundMoney(simpleInterest(e.principal, e.rate, e.fraction),\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:184:supported rule; it is not mishandled by this intentionally restricted example.\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:91:Source symbol-domain intervals are closed; strict bounds use explicit\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:94:host calls; finite schedules/collections come from typed packages. Report\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:120:precision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:124:available; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:125:an unrounded mathematical symbol. The SourceSpan retains the original text.\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:132:an unknown rounding convention.\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:144:| roundMoney | Money<C>, Int, String -> Money<C>; only half_even supported in DemoDebt; rounding at posting boundary, rational ties exact |\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:145:| sumOver | PartitionRef, array of contextual T -> contextual T with that dimension removed; disjoint/exhaustive population proof required |\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:156:## Reconstruction model and finite coverage\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:170:constraints. Branch on finite choices only, with mutually exclusive guards;\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:175:inferred from this finite result.\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:177:Supported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:178:bounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:185:linear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:190:attainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:192:unknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:240:event probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:271:evidence. Exact finite inference is the reference optional method. Continuous\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:331:| bound | formula, query expression, domain, quantisation mode, solver/budget | certified bound/attainment or explicit Unknown/Unbounded |\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:348:linear assertions and finite choices, returns status/witness/core; validate\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:354:grounded in archived interfaces. Only Z3 is exercised by the reference checks.\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:377:  interval additionally needs the declared rounding convention; scale alone\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1380,1410p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nsed -n '1435,1470p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\ncat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\ncat docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json\npython3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/plan-1.response.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nprint('plan verdict:',d['verdict'])\nprint('revision steps:')\nfor i in [1,2,5,7]: print(d['steps'][i])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1380,1410p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nsed -n '1435,1470p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\ncat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\ncat docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json\npython3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/plan-1.response.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nprint('plan verdict:',d['verdict'])\nprint('revision steps:')\nfor i in [1,2,5,7]: print(d['steps'][i])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"            field_rows.append({\"name\": name, \"expression\": info[0]})\n        self.ir[\"contracts\"].append({\"id\": contract.name, \"type\": f\"{package.id}/{contract.type_name}\",\n                                      \"book\": contract.book, \"fields\": field_rows, \"package\": package.id,\n                                      \"source_refs\": [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][1]]})\n        alt_ids = []\n        constraint_ids = []\n        for alt in self.alternatives.values():\n            meta = self.bindings.alternative(alt.name)\n            alt_ids.append(alt.name)\n            alt_constraints = []\n            for index, assumption in enumerate(alt.assumptions):\n                eid = self.lower_expr(assumption, f\"alternative:{alt.name}\", f\"assumption:{index}\")[0]\n                cid = f\"constraint:{_clean_id(alt.name)}:{index}\"\n                self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": cid, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n                                                \"scope\": alt.name, \"source_refs\": []})\n                alt_constraints.append(cid)\n                self._assumption_row(f\"alternative:{alt.name}:{index}\", eid, alt.name, evidence)\n            if not alt_constraints:\n                self.fail(\"MissingAlternativeCondition\", \"named alternatives require a Boolean condition\", alt.name)\n            self.ir[\"alternatives\"].append({\n                \"id\": alt.name, \"parent\": f\"history:{_clean_id(self.model_id)}\", \"scope\": model_scope,\n                \"author\": meta.author,\n                \"created_at\": meta.created_at,\n                \"constraints\": alt_constraints, \"choice_group\": None,\n                \"reason\": meta.reason, \"evidence\": [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][1]],\n                \"opposing_evidence\": [],\n            })\n        for con in self.constraints.values():\n            eid = self.lower_expr(con.expression, f\"constraint:{con.name}\", \"condition\")[0]\n            self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": con.name, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n                                           \"scope\": model_scope, \"source_refs\": []})\n        if total != 0:\n            self.fail(\"UnbalancedState\", \"opening signed balances must sum to zero\", opening_decl.name)\n        self.ir[\"states\"].append({\"id\": opening_decl.name, \"date\": _iso(opening.date, opening_decl.name),\n                                   \"book\": opening_decl.book,\n                                   \"balances\": [{\"account\": name, \"signed_amount\": rational(value)} for name, value in opening.balances],\n                                   \"contracts\": [contract.name], \"measurements\": [],\n                                   \"dependencies\": list(opening.dependencies) or [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][2]]})\n        report = next(iter(self.reports.values()))\n        rb = self.bindings.report(report.mapping.key if isinstance(report.mapping, External) else str(report.mapping)) if isinstance(report.mapping, External) else None\n        if rb is None:\n            self.fail(\"UnsupportedReportMapping\", \"report mapping must be an explicit external binding\", report.name)\n        self.ir[\"reportMappings\"].append({\"id\": report.name, \"book\": report.book, \"basis\": package.id,\n                                          \"rows\": [{\"name\": \"package_mapping\", \"expression\": self._source_ref_expr(rb.mapping, report.name)}],\n                                          \"closing_policy\": f\"{package.id}/{rb.closing_policy}\",\n                                          \"cash_flow_policy\": f\"{package.id}/{rb.cash_flow_policy}\",\n                                          \"required_operations\": [f\"{package.id}/{x}\" for x in rb.required_operations]})\n        # Profile scope and conservative family status.  This profile does not\n        # perform a reconstruction or feasibility search.\n        slot = self._literal_expr(\"scope\", \"slot_limit\", 1, \"Int\")\n        self.ir[\"modelScopes\"].append({\"id\": model_scope, \"templates\": [f\"{package.id}/{contract.type_name}\"],\n                                       \"slot_limits\": [{\"name\": \"debt_contracts\", \"expression\": slot}],\n                                       \"resolution\": \"one fixed/floating aggregate, annual simple accrual\",\n                                       \"calendars\": [self.bindings.calendar_id], \"choices\": [],\n                                       \"exclusions\": [\"fees\", \"foreign_currency\", \"embedded_options\"], \"obligations\": []})\n        family_id = f\"history:{_clean_id(self.model_id)}\"\n        self.ir[\"historyFamilies\"].append({\"id\": family_id, \"scope\": model_scope,\n            \"evidence_view\": evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][2], \"opening_state\": opening_decl.name,\n            \"symbols\": list(self.symbols), \"choices\": [], \"constraints\": constraint_ids,\n            \"alternatives\": alt_ids, \"feasibility\": \"Unknown\", \"coverage\": \"PartialSearch\",\n            \"completed_cells\": 0, \"unresolved_cells\": 1, \"witnesses\": [], \"solver_results\": []})\n        declarations = [self.let_ids.get(n, n) for n in self.decls]\n        declarations = [n for n in declarations if n not in self.sources]\n        self.ir[\"models\"].append({\"id\": self.model_id, \"language_version\": \"Core0.1\",\n                                  \"declarations\": list(dict.fromkeys(declarations)),\n                                  \"package_lock\": [package.id], \"scope\": model_scope})\n        self.ir[\"expressions\"] = list(self.expr_rows.values())\nmodule BorrowingExample version \"1\";\nuse DemoDebt version \"1\";\nsource note7 = external(\"synthetic-note-7\");\nentity Acme functional USD;\nbook Local entity Acme basis DemoDebt version \"1\";\naccount Cash : Asset book Local;\naccount Debt : Liability book Local;\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Local;\naccount Retained : Equity book Local;\nopening after2025 for Local from external(\"after-2025-close\");\nobservation debt : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 100 USD from note7;\nsymbol alpha : Real in [0, 1] because \"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\";\ncontract loans : DebtMix book Local {\n  principal = value(debt);\n  fixed_fraction = alpha;\n  fixed_rate = 0.05 per year;\n  initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\n}\nalternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\nalternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\nscenario rateShock { set market_rate = constant(0.07 per year); }\nreport statements for Local { mapping = external(\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\"); }\n{\n  \"exact\": {\n    \"principal\": \"100\",\n    \"historical_rate\": \"0.05\",\n    \"historical_interest\": \"5\",\n    \"fixed_rate\": \"0.05\",\n    \"stress_rate\": \"0.07\",\n    \"cash\": \"95\",\n    \"equity\": \"-5\",\n    \"expected\": {\n      \"fixed_interest\": \"5\",\n      \"floating_interest\": \"7\",\n      \"fixed_cash\": \"90\",\n      \"floating_cash\": \"88\",\n      \"fixed_equity\": \"-10\",\n      \"floating_equity\": \"-12\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"rounded\": {\n    \"debt\": [\n      \"99.5\",\n      \"100.5\"\n    ],\n    \"interest\": [\n      \"4.5\",\n      \"5.5\"\n    ],\n    \"interval\": \"lower closed, upper open\",\n    \"constraints\": [\n      \"F>=0\",\n      \"V>=0\",\n      \"99.5<=F+V<100.5\",\n      \"4.5<=0.05*(F+V)<5.5\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_infimum\": \"4.975\",\n    \"expected_infimum_attained\": true,\n    \"expected_supremum\": \"7.035\",\n    \"expected_supremum_attained\": false\n  },\n  \"mixture\": {\n    \"hypotheses\": [\n      \"fixed\",\n      \"floating\"\n    ],\n    \"prior\": [\n      \"0.6\",\n      \"0.4\"\n    ],\n    \"likelihood_new_evidence\": [\n      \"0.2\",\n      \"0.8\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_posterior\": [\n      \"3/11\",\n      \"8/11\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_stress_mean\": \"5.8\",\n    \"partial_failure\": {\n      \"fixed\": \"complete\",\n      \"floating\": \"unsupported\",\n      \"successful_mass\": \"0.6\",\n      \"unresolved_mass\": \"0.4\",\n      \"unconditional_mean\": \"unavailable\"\n    }\n  }\n}\nplan verdict: PLAN\nrevision steps:\n2. Add scripts/reconstruction_v1.py with versioned inputs/results and explicit validation of registry templates, openings, slots, contextual observations, admissions, mappings and budgets. Distinguish three records: parent-family constraints P; named conditional predicates A_i; genuine finite choices. The P03 adapter consumes validated IR plus explicit template bindings, preserves provenance, and maps choice_group=null alternatives to named views only. Parent queries use P; selecting a view uses P AND A_i without mutating P. Multiple-view intersection or union requires an explicit query operator. Neither exclusivity, exhaustiveness nor weights follow from labels.\n3. Construct constraints from inputs. Instantiate each declared slot once with activation and nonnegative amount; inactive implies zero. Derive dated roll-forwards and report expressions from posting incidence and economic-state coefficients. Share symbols by economic IDs and attach each accepted observation domain once with source/assumption IDs. Keep view predicates outside parent constraints and the choice enumeration. Genuine choice guards apply jointly across accounts/dates. For overlapping Boolean guards, create disjoint decision-prefix cells, preserving their exact union; verify disjointness and coverage or leave coverage uncertified. Preserve unmatched obligations and explicit scope exclusions.\n6. Preserve joint queries and unfinished work. Coverage counts genuine choice/partition/integer cells, never conditional-view labels; a parent with no genuine choices has one symbolic cell despite multiple views. Each conditional query gets separate scope and coverage metadata. Record total, completed, feasible, infeasible and unresolved cells with a defined counting convention. Enforce slot, formula-size, integer-assignment, cell, solver-resource and elapsed-time limits; retain unvisited regions compactly. Feasible witnesses may coexist with PartialSearch. Infeasible requires all relevant cells proved infeasible; ExactWithinScope additionally requires all applicable obligations resolved or explicitly outside scope. Partial-cell extrema remain explored bounds. Preserve formulas and branch identities, testing joint output tuples against shared constraints.\n8. Implement tests/test_accounting_p04.py and independent oracles using small known-history fixtures plus selected immutable Northstar and borrowing inputs. Independently replay templates to generate observations, withholding hidden histories and authored expected constraints from production reconstruction. Compare complete finite sets and analytic continuous bounds. Include the parent/interior, isolated conditional-query and overlapping-view integration assertions listed in checks; endpoint extrema alone cannot establish preservation of the parent family. Tie every fixture obligation to executed assertions and include metamorphic input changes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '156,203p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\nsed -n '136,154p' docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex\nsed -n '1453,1470p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nsed -n '82p;94p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '156,203p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\nsed -n '136,154p' docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex\nsed -n '1453,1470p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nsed -n '82p;94p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Reconstruction model and finite coverage\n\nA ModelScope lists templates, slots per entity/period, books, account roles,\ntiming/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\noperations. A slot is a possible aggregate event, with an active flag and\nnonnegative amount; inactive implies zero. A template declares both its posting\nincidence vector and economic-state change. Sales and collections are different\nslots; issue and reset are different slots. Debt states retain F/V, rates,\nreset calendar, maturity and hedge links even when historical incidence agrees.\n\nInstantiate every declared slot once, then share variables by economic IDs and\nobservation IDs. Compile roll-forwards and report mappings into constraints;\nadd each accepted evidence domain once. Match source observations by exact\ncontext/mapping, never by label similarity. Attach source/assumption IDs to\nconstraints. Branch on finite choices only, with mutually exclusive guards;\ncontinuous families remain formulas. Count completed, infeasible and unresolved\nchoice cells. `ExactWithinScope` requires every cell decided and each matching\nsource obligation resolved or explicitly outside simulation scope. A satisfied\nwitness alone does not establish coverage. Real-world completeness is never\ninferred from this finite result.\n\nSupported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\nbounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\nMoney quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\nminor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\nand nonlinear constraints may not be silently submitted as continuous LPs.\nUnknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\nfunctions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\nFixed proportions times known totals are linear; variable F,V with F+V=D is\nlinear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\nproved D>0 becomes F>=aD; an unknown a restores bilinearity.\n\nFeasibility results are sat+exact witness, unsat+constraint/source core or\nunknown+reason+undecided formula. Bounds include lower/upper rational value,\nattainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ninequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\nunknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\ntimeout preserves undecided cells rather than deleting them.\n\n## Temporal selection and local review\n\nAn EvidenceView first filters by availability cutoff and (if requested)\ningestion cutoff. Day-only availability maps to the next local midnight using\nthe named timezone; finer availability requires evidence. Selective explicit\nsupersession removes only the targeted assertions in the same context. A\nsuperseding assertion must be eligible itself. Transitive successors follow\nthe acyclic supersession graph. Competing maximal assertions form a conflict\nset, never a last-row-wins result. Original view chooses initial assertions in\nscenario rateShock {\n  set market_rate = constant(0.07 per year);\n}\n\\end{lstlisting}\n\nThe parent model retains every $\\alpha\\in[0,1]$. The two named alternatives\nare useful conditional views of that family, not a declaration that the\nendpoints exhaust it. Requesting the parent family's exact bounds produces\n$[5,7]$ for the next year's expense in this simple model. Requesting a\nconditional run of \\code{allFixed} supplies $\\alpha=1$. Requesting a weighted\nmixture requires a separate weight model; the two labels do not create equal\nweights.\n\nAn observation declaration is a reference to evidence plus a proposed typed\nreading. The compiler checks that the registry context agrees with the declared\nperiod and type. If the evidence is rounded, \\code{value(debt)} denotes a\nshared constrained value rather than a silently exact 100. This synthetic\nregistry explicitly declares an exact value, which keeps the illustration\ndeterministic.\n        slot = self._literal_expr(\"scope\", \"slot_limit\", 1, \"Int\")\n        self.ir[\"modelScopes\"].append({\"id\": model_scope, \"templates\": [f\"{package.id}/{contract.type_name}\"],\n                                       \"slot_limits\": [{\"name\": \"debt_contracts\", \"expression\": slot}],\n                                       \"resolution\": \"one fixed/floating aggregate, annual simple accrual\",\n                                       \"calendars\": [self.bindings.calendar_id], \"choices\": [],\n                                       \"exclusions\": [\"fees\", \"foreign_currency\", \"embedded_options\"], \"obligations\": []})\n        family_id = f\"history:{_clean_id(self.model_id)}\"\n        self.ir[\"historyFamilies\"].append({\"id\": family_id, \"scope\": model_scope,\n            \"evidence_view\": evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][2], \"opening_state\": opening_decl.name,\n            \"symbols\": list(self.symbols), \"choices\": [], \"constraints\": constraint_ids,\n            \"alternatives\": alt_ids, \"feasibility\": \"Unknown\", \"coverage\": \"PartialSearch\",\n            \"completed_cells\": 0, \"unresolved_cells\": 1, \"witnesses\": [], \"solver_results\": []})\n        declarations = [self.let_ids.get(n, n) for n in self.decls]\n        declarations = [n for n in declarations if n not in self.sources]\n        self.ir[\"models\"].append({\"id\": self.model_id, \"language_version\": \"Core0.1\",\n                                  \"declarations\": list(dict.fromkeys(declarations)),\n                                  \"package_lock\": [package.id], \"scope\": model_scope})\n        self.ir[\"expressions\"] = list(self.expr_rows.values())\n| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
